NAME
       cfm - file manager

SYNOPSIS
       cfm [directory]

DESCRIPTION
       A full-screen file manager: the listing on the left, a preview
       on the right. Text files are previewed as text, directories as
       their contents, and images are drawn on the framebuffer.
       Animated GIFs play in the preview panel as soon as they are
       selected, and full screen when opened.

KEYS
       arrows, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End   move around
       Enter, right   open (directory, or view the file)
       Backspace, left   go up
       e        run the selected file
       r        rename          d   delete
       c        copy            x   cut          v, p   paste
       g        re-read the directory
       n        make a directory
       o        open with another program
       y        copy the path to the clipboard
       .        show hidden files
       s        settings
       q        quit

       Up at the top of the listing wraps to the bottom, and down at
       the bottom wraps back to the top.

OPEN WITH
       o offers the programs that suit the selected file - play for a
       song, img for a picture, neo to edit it, less to read it - and
       runs the one you pick. A directory is not offered anything.

SETTINGS
       s opens the settings. Left and right change a value.

         Preview pane     show the panel on the right at all
         Confirm delete   ask before deleting
         Show hidden      list names beginning with a dot
         Sort by          name, size or type
         Sort order       ascending or descending
         Folders first    keep directories above files, however sorted
         Show dates       a modification-time column in the listing
         Preview width    how much of the screen the panel takes
         Animate GIFs     play them in the panel, or show frame one
         Confirm quit     ask before leaving
         Save settings    write them to ~/.cfmrc

       ~/.cfmrc is read at startup, so the settings survive a reboot on
       an installed system.

FILES
       ~/.cfmrc

SEE ALSO
       neo(1), img(1), ls(1), play(1), copy(1), paste(1)
